; dsv4-decode-form-band.fk — what the Form-held DS4 decode loop can actually stand on today.
;
; PROOF LEVEL: METAL-LINKED fkwu ONLY. This band drives a real GPU through the handle door and reads a
; real 9.1 GB GGUF, so it has exactly one home arm — the repo-root fkwu, Metal linked automatically
; by validate.sh's own build_fkwu_src on Darwin:
;     cd .. && ./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/dsv4-decode-form-band.fk
; On any other arm metal_status answers metal_linked=false and bit 1 does not light, which takes the
; whole verdict with it — that is the intended SKIP, and it is spoken rather than silent.
;
; WHAT THIS BAND NOW CLAIMS, AND WHAT IT STILL REFUSES. The 43-layer stack exists
; (native/metal/dsv4-decode-stack.fk) and bit 2^53 holds its greedy STREAM against the receipt-
; recorded ids — token identity over 25 steps, the strongest claim this ladder makes. What is still
; NOT claimed: bit-for-bit logit equality with metal_dsv4_stack.sh (the associations differ where
; each receipt says they differ), any position past 127 (the ratio-128 windows have never closed on
; this device), the indexer mask (inert below 2048 tokens, declared), and SPEED (no bit prices
; ms/token; the floor conversation starts after the ids, quiet). Gaps live in the cells' UNFINISHED
; blocks, not papered.
;
; WHY THE GATE IS metal_status AND NOT A NUMBER. Every other primitive on this door answers an INTEGER
; handle, and an unbound name under axiom-5 recovers to nothing and answers 0. A 0 from a door that was
; never linked, a 0 from a door that refused, and a 0 from a typo are the same shape. metal_status is
; the one primitive whose answer cannot be counterfeited by a numb call, so bit 1 is checked first and
; every later bit is worthless without it.
;
; WHY BIT 2 IS PINNED TO LITERALS AND NOT TO AGREEMENT WITH ITSELF. The cell reads the geometry by
; walking the file's header. Comparing that walk to itself proves nothing: a wrong offset would make
; the GPU and the CPU cross-check read the SAME wrong bytes and agree perfectly. So the five numbers
; below are pinned to what an INDEPENDENT ARM printed — form-kernel-go/bin-go running
; gm-emit-manifest over the same file, which answered:
;     T token_embd.weight 1 2 4096 129280 1 71707886176 529530880 1 1059061760
; Same recipe, different kernel. A literal cannot drift with the code that produced it.
;
; Verdict 2147483647 when the eight rungs are honest:
;   1   the door SPEAKS — metal_status carries metal_linked=true (the voice canary, checked first)
;   2   the geometry is READ FROM THE HEADER and matches the Go arm's manifest literally:
;       n_embd 4096, vocab 129280, ggml type 1 (F16), absolute offset 71707886176, bytes 1059061760
;   4   the weights are the FILE'S OWN PAGES — metal_status reports a nocopy mmap buffer, so the
;       9.1 GB never crossed the host membrane as a copy; reading the model file is the one permitted
;       crossing and this proves it stayed that
;   8   the door ENQUEUED WITHOUT WAITING — the batch was still open when the read drained it
;   16  EVERY lane of the embedding row is bit-exact against this body's own f16->f32 widening,
;       bad=0 AND odd=0 (a fold over all n_embd, no epsilon, no sampling, nothing excused)
;   32  the fp-contract pragma this cell emits ACTUALLY suppresses contraction through this door —
;       checked, not asserted, because the door compiles with options:nil and contracts by default
;  128  RMSNORM ON SYNTHETIC TRUTH, EXACT. x=2.0, g=1.0, eps=0 -> inv must be 0x3F000000 and every
;       lane exactly 0x3F800000. Hand-computed, no tolerance, no tool. The strongest bit in rung 2.
;  256  blk.0.attn_norm.weight sits at the address the Go arm printed (72877251424) and is n_embd wide
;  512  the REDUCE agrees with a Form fp64 fold over the same bytes, via implied mean-square
;       (1/inv^2 - eps), which needs no sqrt on the reference side. Tolerance 1e-6; measured 1.03e-7.
;       GATED on the row address pin — see below.
; 1024  the APPLY agrees with the fp64 reference against the VECTOR'S SCALE (overfine, row 934),
;       not each element's own magnitude. Tolerance 1e-6; measured 6.25e-8. GATED on the row pin AND
;       on bit 256, because the reference reads the norm weights through the same address the GPU got.
;       WITHOUT THOSE GATES BOTH BITS WERE COMOVED AND PROVED NOTHING: mutation N5 (embed the wrong
;       row) answered 2047, and N1 (output_norm.weight in place of blk.0.attn_norm.weight) answered
;       1791 where 767 was predicted. The relative error is only evidence once the addresses are pinned.
; 2048  THE MXFP8 FUSED MATVEC ON SYNTHETIC TRUTH, EXACT. Payload byte 56 (E4M3 1.0) and scale byte
;       127 (E8M0 2^0 = 1.0) with x = 1.0 gives y[r] = cols = 4096.0 = 0x45800000 on every row, and
;       every partial sum is an integer below 2^24 so it is exact under ANY association. That is the
;       bit's strength and its stated limit: it proves the decode, the scale-plane origin at nel, and
;       that every column was visited exactly once -- and it is BLIND to association, which is what
;       ds4-order-match.fk exists for. Bit 8192 is not its evidence and it is not bit 8192's.
; 4096  blk.0.attn_q_a.weight is where the Go arm said (72838323040), type 41, 1024x4096. The file's
;       own byte count 4325376 equals nel + nel/32, so the plane-split layout is confirmed by
;       arithmetic before any kernel reads it.
; 8192  the real projection (embed -> rmsnorm -> MXFP8 matvec, four dispatches, ONE sync) agrees with
;       the body's own mxp8-at reader folded in fp64 over eight rows, judged against the ROW VECTOR'S
;       SCALE. Measured 68 ppb. Per ELEMENT the same disagreement reads 1018 ppb purely because
;       y[0] = 0.017 is a near-cancellation of terms of scale 0.1 -- overfine, row 934, is exactly
;       this case. GATED on bit 4096 and on the row pin. EIGHT rows of 1024, because each is a
;       4096-term fp64 fold in Form; a fault confined to high row indices would not be seen.
; 16384 THE FOLD-ORDER WITNESS, the bit the uniform synthetics cannot be. Weights 1.0, x[0] = 2^24,
;       x[1..31] = 1.0, rest 0. fp64 truth is 2^24+31; the kernel's stated ascending in-group fold
;       lands each +1 on a tie-to-even that rounds BACK to 2^24, so the f32 answer is EXACTLY
;       0x4B800000 — and a reversed or pairwise fold answers 2^24+32, sixteen bits away. Verified by
;       f32-step simulation before the kernel ran. From the attention split onward order is the whole
;       question (ds4-order-match.fk), and this is the reusable instrument for it.
; 32768 rung-4 geometry, all four tensors at the Go arm's addresses: q_a_norm 72766950240,
;       kv_a_norm 72766948192, q_b 72842648416 [32768 x 1024], kv 72766954336.
; 65536 both rank-space rmsnorms agree with the fp64 reference (tn-sqrt, the body's Newton spine):
;       measured 120 ppb (q, n=1024) and 77 ppb (k, n=512) against the vector's scale.
; 131072 the q_b projection (type 41, 8 of 32768 rows) agrees: measured 178 ppb.
; 262144 headrms over ALL 64 heads agrees: measured 429 ppb — above the other steps because the
;       kernel's mla_sqrt is f32 Newton against the reference's fp64 Newton, still 2000x under the
;       bar. The chain is covered by induction: each step's reference reads the GPU's INPUT for that
;       step (the previous step's separately-checked output buffer) and weights at pinned addresses.
; 524288 blk.0.attn_sinks.weight at the Go arm's 72766947936, AND freqs[0] == 0x3F800000 exactly —
;       pow(base, 0) = 1 is an identity of the function, not a tolerance. The freqs are computed ON
;       THE DEVICE by a cell-emitted kernel and read back; the fp64 rope reference widens those same
;       bits, so a wrong pow cannot agree its way past this bit.
; 1048576 RoPE at pos 7: the NOPE dims (448 per head, k row + q head 0) are BIT-EQUAL through the
;       kernel — a copy is checked as a copy — and the rotated tails agree with fcos/fsin in fp64:
;       measured 236 ppb against the tail's scale. Layer 0 is a ratio-0 raw-regime layer; the
;       compressed-base reduction (layer 2+) is NOT claimed by this bit.
; 2097152 the sink-softmax attention (one KV row, 64 heads) agrees with mla-attn.fk's softmax shape
;       folded in fp64 (tn-exp, tn-sqrt): measured 886 ppb — the widest step yet because mla_exp is
;       an f32 Taylor against fp64, still under the bar. scale = 1/sqrt(512) rides as f32 bits
;       1026884851; the reference derives its own from tn-sqrt, so the literal is cross-checked.
; 4194304 rung-6 geometry, both attention-exit tensors at the Go arm's addresses on the canonical
;       imatrix file: output_a 78989329472 [8192 x 4096] and output_b 79024981056 [4096 x 8192],
;       both type 8 (Q8_0, 35651584 bytes = rows*cols/32*34 exactly), AND the grouping rank DERIVED
;       from that pinned geometry as rows*cols/hu_len = 8192*4096/32768 = 1024 — never a constant
;       taken on faith.
; 8388608 the INVERSE rope (the attention exit's un-rotation, oracle: gpuRope(ha,...,true)): the
;       NOPE dims of heads 0 and 63 are BIT-EQUAL through the kernel (896 of 896) and the rotated
;       tails agree with fcos/fsin in fp64 at the NEGATED angle (sign=-1 multiplies only sin, which
;       IS angle negation): measured 194 ppb. GATED on the chain pins and on bit 524288, because the
;       reference widens the freqs the DEVICE computed.
; 16777216 the GROUPED output_a projection (dsv4-forward-real.fk's own Q8_0 grouped kernel text,
;       compiled in process): eight rows sampled ON BOTH SIDES of group seams {0,1, 1024,1025,
;       4096,4097, 7168,7169} agree with the body's q80-flat-at reader folded in fp64, each row
;       reading its (r/rank)-th 4096-wide slice of the GPU's actual inverse-roped buffer: measured
;       114 ppb. GATED on bit 4194304 — the reference reads weights at the PINNED address.
; 33554432 the output_b projection closing the attention block (type 8, eight sampled rows of
;       8192-term fp64 folds, input = the GPU's actual grouped output): measured 108 ppb. GATED on
;       bit 4194304 and the chain pins. attn_out[0] printed by the run: 1.559525.
; 67108864 THE KV ROUND ON SYNTHETIC TRUTH, EXACT, the tie rule on the knife edge. Group 0 carries
;       amax=448 so the scale is exactly 1 and the E4M3FN ladder is bare: 1.0625 (exact midpoint of
;       indices 56/57, best even, STAYS -> 1.0) and 1.1875 (midpoint of 57/58, best odd, MOVES ->
;       1.25) pin ds4.c's tie-to-even-INDEX in both directions; 448 pins the top magnitude; the
;       all-zero groups pin the amax floor; the tail pins the f16-only path. Hand-computed bits.
; 134217728 the real roped K row rounds BIT-EXACTLY (512 of 512 lanes) against a Form fp64
;       reference on format-arith's fq- spine — a different text from the MSL. Every reference step
;       is exact in fp64 over f32 inputs (power-of-two scales, exactly-representable magnitudes,
;       Sterbenz-exact ladder distances); the ONE f32 rounding the kernel performs that fp64 does
;       not share (amax/448.0f) is emulated with fq-quant(...,23). So this bit is equality, not a
;       tolerance. The attend (bit 2097152) now reads the ROUNDED row, as ds4.c:3211 places it —
;       its reference reads the same buffer the GPU's attend read.
; 268435456 THE GROWING KV CACHE OVER A REAL PROMPT. "The capital of France is" -> ids 671 6102
;       294 8760 344 (the body's own tokenizer cell, the one authority). Each position runs the k
;       chain AT ITS OWN POSITION and the folded checks are per position: embed bit-exact at the
;       id's PINNED row address (77928033088 + id*8192, five literals), kv matvec vs fp64 at two
;       sampled rows, rope NOPE/tails at pos t (t=0 is the identity and the check knows it), and
;       the fp8+f16 round bit-exact 512/512. The intermediate buffers are REUSED serially — nine
;       dispatches a position — and the rounded row is appended by a cell-emitted copy kernel.
; 536870912 CACHE ASSEMBLY: every cache row is bit-equal to the snapshot taken from the round's
;       output buffer the moment that position finished. This bit owns WHERE the append wrote;
;       a rotated row index drops it while everything else stays green.
; 1073741824 the sink-softmax attention over ALL FIVE ROWS (nrows=5, gpuAttendSplit's arithmetic at
;       nComp=0) agrees with the fp64 multi-row reference (tn-exp/tn-sqrt, 8 sampled heads, every
;       row): measured 882 ppb. Deliberately NOT gated on the assembly bit — it tests attend on the
;       ACTUAL cache (induction), and a misplaced row is the assembly bit's to catch.
;   64  the token's row lands at the absolute address an INDEPENDENT computation says it must:
;       71707886176 + 671*4096*2 = 77933529920. THIS BIT WAS ADDED BECAUSE THE BAND FAILED A
;       MUTATION WITHOUT IT (M2, embed the wrong row: predicted 47, band answered 63). bit16 now
;       depends on it, so a perfect fold over the wrong row can no longer read green.
;
; ── RUNG 9: the SECOND cache on blk.2, the first ratio-4 layer, over EIGHT real positions ──
; 2147483648 (2^31) rung-9 geometry, every blk.2 tensor at the Go arm's address on the canonical
;       file: compressor kv 79283669056 / gate 79275280448 / ape 79275270208 (1024x4 — width
;       coff*hd = 2*512 and ratio 4 confirmed by the tensor's own dims) / norm 79275278400 (512),
;       attn_norm 79427201600, attn_kv 79313562176, q_a 79387093568, q_b 79391550016, sinks
;       79275269952, compressor projections type 1 (F16).
; 4294967296 (2^32) the YaRN table, computed ON the device, pinned at four regimes: freqs[0] ==
;       0x3F800000 exactly (identity); freqs[1] vs fpow(160000, -1/32) in Form fp64 (below the
;       ramp — pure pow, and 160000 is the file's own compress_rope_freq_base); freqs[20] vs
;       fpow(160000,-20/32) * 0.53125 (INSIDE the ramp: y=0.5, factor 0.0625*0.5+0.5 — a wrong
;       lo/hi/fscale moves it); freqs[25] vs fpow(160000,-25/32) * 0.0625 (past the ramp — pure
;       interpolation). lo=15/hi=25 derived from the file's yarn scalars, corr() far from integers.
; 8589934592 (2^33) the raw lane at layer 2 over the eight positions of the RECORDED tokenization
;       "The capital of France is..." -> 671 6102 294 8760 344 11111 305 270 (the body's own
;       tokenizer, receipts/2026-07-22-tokenizer-speed.md): per position embed bit-exact at the
;       PINNED row address (eight literals below), kv matvec vs fp64 at two rows, rope at TRUE pos
;       with the COMPRESSED-base table (ropeFreqs(il) — a ratio layer's raw k IS roped base-160000),
;       round bit-exact 512/512.
; 17179869184 (2^34) the compressor projections (F16 serial ascending fold) BIT-EQUAL to the exact
;       f32-fold emulation (fq-quant per step) over the file's bytes at the pinned addresses and
;       the GPU's own xn — 32 sampled rows. Measured 4499 ppb against plain fp64 first: a serial
;       4096-term f32 fold accumulates ~n*eps, so the bar was not loosened, the check was UPGRADED
;       to bit equality. An fma (pragma failure) or a reordered fold lands on different bits.
;       GATED on 2^31.
; 34359738368 (2^35) BOTH pooled rows agree with dsv4-compressor.fk's RECIPE (band 2047) folded in
;       fp64 — the state machine evolved entirely on the Form side, fed the GPU's own projections
;       (anchored by 2^34) and the ape read from the FILE, so a wrong device row index, ape column,
;       candidate offset, or missing shift cannot move both sides together. The ratio-4 eight-
;       candidate two-lane trap is exactly what this bit holds. Measured 160 ppb. GATED on 2^31+2^34.
; 68719476736 (2^36) the emitted row finishes exactly as compStep says: comp norm vs fp64 (82 ppb),
;       rope at comp_pos = pos+1-ratio with the DEVICE's YaRN freqs — window 2 lands comp_pos 4, a
;       real angle — NOPE 448/448 bit-equal, tails 113 ppb; the fp8+f16 round bit-exact 512/512;
;       and the comp cache assembly bit-equal to the round's own output per window. GATED on
;       2^31 + 2^32 (the rope reference widens the freqs the device computed).
; 137438953472 (2^37) ONE softmax over the raw window AND the compressed rows —
;       form_mla_attend_mixed_f32, nrows=8 ncomp=2 — vs the fp64 multi-row reference over the
;       CONCATENATED planes (attend_mixed's fold order IS the concatenation's): 4 sampled heads,
;       all 10 rows, measured 322 ppb. GATED on 2^31 (the sinks pin rides there).
;
; ── RUNG 10: the MoE — both routing regimes, the experts, the shared lane, at token 671 ──
; 274877906944 (2^38) rung-10 geometry, every FFN tensor at the Go arm's address on the canonical
;       file: gate/up/down exps 14641984 / 1272933184 / 568290112 (types 16/10, dim2 256 — the
;       tensor's own, never the metadata), gate_inp 79100757056, ffn_norm 79129592896, tid2eid
;       5333824, shexp g/u/d 79102854208 / 79120680000 / 79111767104, blk.3 gate_inp/bias/ffn_norm
;       79579828288 / 79579827264 / 79608664128, N_FF 2048, and the per-expert strides BY ARITHMETIC:
;       553648128/256 = 2162688 (IQ2_XXS) and 704643072/256 = 2752512 (Q2_K — the stride whose
;       0-pricing once sent every expert to expert 0's bytes; gm-priced? owns that lesson).
; 549755813888 (2^39) the router logits: gate_inp is F16 and the serial fold is EMULATED bit-exactly
;       (rung 9's instrument) on the six SELECTED rows plus rows 0 and 255. GATED on 2^38.
; 1099511627776 (2^40) HASH routing (forepick): the six ids the GPU's table read returned are the
;       file's own I32 row for token 671, pinned as LITERALS read independently of this cell
;       (raw bytes at 5333824 + 671*24): 147 78 30 248 217 179; expert 147's slice address
;       14641984 + 147*2162688 = 332557120 pinned by arithmetic; probs = sqrt(softplus) vs fp64
;       (157 ppb measured); weights within 4 ulp of the exact emulation — 4 ulp is DERIVED, not
;       negotiated: this door and the oracle's own metallibs both run Metal fast-math division
;       (<= 2.5 ulp), so bit equality through a division is the wrong instrument on both.
; 2199023255552 (2^41) the routed experts' gate/up (IQ2_XXS, iq2xxs-dequant.fk's carver in fp64,
;       two sampled rows per slot, both stacks — 325/244 ppb) and the clamped SwiGLU (dsv4-forward's
;       own recipe, 98 ppb) INCLUDING the clamp witnessed ON DEVICE: gate=up=12 > lim=10 must land
;       on the clamped value and sit 0.1%+ from the unclamped one. GATED on 2^40 (the references
;       read the GPU's own ids).
; 4398046511104 (2^42) the down projection (Q2_K, q2k-dequant.fk's carver, slot-strided x — 611 ppb)
;       and the reduce EMULATED bit-exactly (ascending f32 over six slot planes, all 4096 dims).
; 8796093022208 (2^43) the shared lane: three Q8_0 projections vs q80-flat-at in fp64 (107 ppb), the
;       shared SwiGLU at w=1 (94 ppb), and the final moe+shared add EMULATED bit-exactly (all 4096).
; 17592186044416 (2^44) the LEARNED regime on blk.3: logits bit-equal (4 rows), probs vs fp64
;       (296 ppb), sc = probs + bias bit-equal all 256 (bias from the FILE's own bytes), the tg6
;       SELECTION reproduced by the kernel's own scan (strict >, first-index-wins) over the GPU's
;       own sc — six ids EQUAL — and the weights within the same derived 4-ulp bound, computed from
;       PROBS and never sc: the bias enters the selection and never the weight (ds4.c:10665's
;       asymmetry, the thing moe-gate.fk cannot stand in for).
;
; ── RUNG 11: the hyper-connection frame at blk.0 (attn side), real weights, HC_ITERS=20 ──
; 35184372088832 (2^45) rung-11 geometry: hc_attn fn/scale/base at 79129609376 / 79130395808 /
;       79129609280 (fn [16384 x 24] F16), and the ffn frame's three pinned beside them for the
;       single-layer rung: 79130395936 / 79131182368 / 79130395840.
; 70368744177664 (2^46) the input chain: broadcast bit-equal (a copy checked as a copy, 16384/16384),
;       the no-weight wide rmsnorm vs fp64 (100 ppb), and the fn matvec (F16 serial) EMULATED
;       bit-exactly on ALL 24 rows. GATED on 2^45.
; 140737488355328 (2^47) the SPLIT: sigmoid pre/post + the 20-iteration Sinkhorn vs dsv4-hc.fk's
;       recipe (band 63) in fp64 — measured 104 ppb: the Sinkhorn CONVERGES, so twenty iterations
;       do not accumulate — and the post/comb slice copies bit-equal. iters rides as a runtime
;       uniform (edgedrop: an unrun iteration is not a computed zero). GATED on 2^45 + 2^46.
; 281474976710656 (2^48) wsum and hc_post EMULATED bit-exactly (all 4096 / all 16384), the post
;       including the TRANSPOSE read comb[dst + src*n_hc] (ds4.c:9786) — asymmetric real weights, so
;       a wrong transpose cannot hide (dsv4-hc-msl.fk's edgedrop lesson). GATED on 2^45.
;
; ── RUNG 12: the EXIT HEAD (hc collapse -> output_norm -> output.weight), head arithmetic only ──
; 562949953421312 (2^49) rung-12 geometry: output_hc fn/scale/base 86157337440 / 86157468512 /
;       86157337408 (fn [16384 x 4] F16), output_norm 86720095104, output.weight 86157468544
;       (Q8_0, vocab 129280 — the tensor's own dim).
; 1125899906842624 (2^50) the collapse chain: rmsnorm-nw vs fp64 (100 ppb), the output_hc_fn matvec
;       EMULATED bit-exactly (all 4 rows over 16384), headw sigmoid vs fp64 (85 ppb), the wsum
;       collapse EMULATED bit-exactly (4096/4096). GATED on 2^49. The residual is
;       broadcast(embed) — a DECLARED stand-in; the model's own argmax is NOT claimed by this rung.
; 2251799813685248 (2^51) the exit: output_norm through the reduce/apply pair vs fp64 (30/58 ppb)
;       and the Q8_0 unembedding vs q80-flat-at in fp64 at eight rows INCLUDING the argmax row and
;       the runner-up (136 ppb). GATED on 2^49.
;
; ── RUNG 13: ONE COMPLETE LAYER end to end (blk.0, pos 0, token 671) ──
; 4503599627370496 (2^52) the JOIN: broadcast -> hcPre(attn) -> MLA -> hcPost -> hcPre(ffn) ->
;       ffn_norm -> MoE + shared -> hcPost, every seam checked against the GPU's actual upstream
;       buffers by the machinery rungs 4-12 proved: attn wsum bit-equal 4096, attn_norm 210 ppb,
;       kv round 512/512, attend 1134 ppb, output_b 146 ppb, attn hcPost bit-equal 16384, ffn wsum
;       bit-equal 4096, ffn_norm 57 ppb, iq2 gate 208 ppb, reduce/add/out-post bit-equal, both
;       Sinkhorn splits vs recipe (104/136 ppb). GATED on 2^38 and 2^45 (the pins that own these
;       tensors). THE ATTEND BAR IS 4e-6 AND DERIVED, NOT NEGOTIATED: mla_exp is a 14-term f32
;       Taylor with argument halving (~20 roundings) against a fp64 reference of the same series —
;       rungs 5/8 measured 886/882 ppb on other inputs, always ~90% of the generic 1e-6 bar; the
;       reduction crosses simd_sum whose hardware tree is not reliably emulable, so a tolerance is
;       the honest instrument and its size comes from the series, not from the miss.
;
; ── RUNG 14: the 43-LAYER STACK and the GREEDY STREAM (native/metal/dsv4-decode-stack.fk) ──
; 9007199254740992 (2^53) the stream: prompt 671 6102 294 8760 344 through the whole stack — 43
;       layers x two hyper-connection frames, both caches, both routing regimes, the shared lane,
;       the exit head — 25 greedy steps, ONE batch and ONE sync per generated token, diffed
;       against the receipt-recorded ids (receipts/2026-07-30-order-match.md): 24 of ds4 own plus
;       the bash lane 25th (6102). 25/25 or dark.
;
; preludes: native/metal/dsv4-decode-stack.fk

(do
    (defn dfb-model () "/Users/ursmuff/models/ds4-engine/gguf/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-IQ2XXS-w2Q2K-AProjQ8-SExpQ8-OutQ8-chat-v2-imatrix.gguf")
    (defn dfb-token () 671)

    ; bit 1 — the voice canary. str_find answers -1 when absent, so a numb door cannot light this.
    (defn dfb-linked? (st) (if (ge (str_find st "metal_linked=true" 0) 0) 1 0))
    (defn dfb-nocopy? (st) (if (ge (str_find st "mmap_nocopy_buffers=0" 0) 0) 0 1))
    ; the read drains the batch, so after it the door must report the dispatches DONE and the batch
    ; empty. pending>0 here would mean the read did not sync; total_dispatch=0 would mean nothing ran.
    (defn dfb-enqueued? (st)
        (if (ge (str_find st "pending=0" 0) 0)
            (if (ge (str_find st "total_dispatch=0" 0) 0) 0 1)
            0))

    (defn dfb-geom? (f)
        (if (eq (nth f 3) 4096)
            (if (eq (nth f 4) 129280)
                (if (eq (nth f 5) 1)
                    (if (eq (nth f 6) 77928033088)
                        (if (eq (nth f 7) 1059061760) 1 0) 0) 0) 0) 0))

    ; bit 64 — THE ROW ITSELF, and this bit exists because the band FAILED a mutation without it.
    ; Mutation M2 made the cell embed token+1 instead of token. Predicted 47; the band answered 63.
    ; It caught nothing, because the reference bytes were read at the SAME computed row offset the
    ; GPU used, so a wrong row moved BOTH sides together and they agreed perfectly about the wrong
    ; place. That is precisely the self-referential trap this band's own header warns about for the
    ; geometry — written down, and then not applied one field over. The cure is the same cure: pin the
    ; row's absolute address to a literal, computed independently of the code under test as
    ;     71707886176 + 671 * 4096 * 2 = 77933529920
    ; A literal cannot drift with the arithmetic that produced it.
    (defn dfb-rowaddr? (f) (if (eq (nth f 9) 77933529920) 1 0))

    ; bit 16 — the fold. ok must equal n_embd exactly AND bad and odd must both be zero AND the row
    ; must be the right row. Demanding all four is the point: ok=n_embd with odd>0 would mean lanes
    ; were skipped rather than passed, and a perfect fold over the WRONG row is worth nothing at all.
    (defn dfb-exact? (f)
        (if (eq (dfb-rowaddr? f) 1)
            (if (eq (nth f 0) (nth f 3))
                (if (eq (nth f 1) 0) (if (eq (nth f 2) 0) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))

    ; ── RUNG 2 anchors. rel1/rel2 are fp32-vs-fp64 MAGNITUDE checks and the tolerance is stated
    ; rather than discovered: measured 103 ppb (reduce) and 63 ppb (apply), which is f32 rounding
    ; scale (f32 eps ~119 ppb) over a 4096-term fold. The bar is 1e-6 — ~10x the observed noise and
    ; ~4 orders below any structural error, which lands at 1e-2 or worse. These are NOT bit-exactness
    ; and this band does not call them that; bit 128 is the exact one.
    (defn dfb-tol () 0.000001)
    (defn dfb-rmsgeom? (f2 n)
        (if (eq (nth f2 2) 79100740672) (if (eq (nth f2 4) n) 1 0) 0))

    (let facts (dfd-embed (dfb-model) (dfb-token)))
    (let st (nth facts 8))
    (let b1  (dfb-linked? st))
    (let b2  (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-geom? facts) 0))
    (let b4  (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-nocopy? st) 0))
    (let b8  (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-enqueued? st) 0))
    (let b16 (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-exact? facts) 0))
    (let b32 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-contract-ok?) 0))
    (let b64 (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-rowaddr? facts) 0))
    (let b128 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-rmsnorm-synth (nth facts 3)) 0))
    (let rung2 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-rmsnorm-rung (dfb-model) (dfb-token)) 0))
    (let b256 (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-rmsgeom? rung2 (nth facts 3)) 0))
    ; bits 512/1024 are GATED ON THE PINNED ADDRESSES, not only on the relative error. A relative
    ; error computed against a reference that read the same wrong bytes is not evidence of anything.
    (let rowpin (if (eq (nth rung2 5) 77933529920) 1 0))
    (let b512 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq rowpin 1) (if (lt (nth rung2 0) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0))
    (let b1024 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq rowpin 1) (if (eq b256 1) (if (lt (nth rung2 1) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    ; ── RUNG 3: the MXFP8 q_a projection
    (let b2048 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mx8-synth 1024 4096) 0))
    (let rung3 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mla-rung (dfb-model) (dfb-token)) 0))
    (let b4096 (if (eq b1 1)
                   (if (eq (nth rung3 1) 79060632640)
                       (if (eq (nth rung3 2) 1024) (if (eq (nth rung3 3) 4096) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let rowpin3 (if (eq (nth rung3 4) 77933529920) 1 0))
    (let b8192 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq b4096 1) (if (eq rowpin3 1)
                   (if (lt (nth rung3 0) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    ; ── RUNG 4: q_a_norm/kv_a_norm, q_b, headrms — and the fold-ORDER witness
    (let b16384 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mx8-ordersynth) 0))
    (let rung4 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mla2-rung (dfb-model) (dfb-token)) 0))
    (let b32768 (if (eq b1 1)
        (if (eq (nth rung4 4) 78987097152)
            (if (eq (nth rung4 5) 78987095104)
                (if (eq (nth rung4 6) 79065089088)
                    (if (eq (nth rung4 7) 78987101248)
                        (if (eq (nth rung4 9) 32768)
                            (if (eq (nth rung4 10) 1024) 1 0) 0) 0) 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let rowpin4 (if (eq (nth rung4 8) 77933529920) 1 0))
    (let gate4 (if (eq b32768 1) rowpin4 0))
    (let b65536 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1)
        (if (lt (nth rung4 0) (dfb-tol)) (if (lt (nth rung4 1) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let b131072 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (lt (nth rung4 2) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0))
    (let b262144 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (lt (nth rung4 3) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0))
    ; ── RUNG 5: RoPE + sink-softmax attention (same chain, four more dispatches)
    ; freqs[1] is pinned against fpow(10000, -1/32) computed IN FORM fp64 — 10000.0 is the file's own
    ; deepseek4.rope.freq_base as the Go arm printed it. Without this, the cell's base literal and the
    ; rope reference are COMOVED: the reference widens the freqs the GPU computed, so a wrong base
    ; agrees with itself perfectly. freqs[0] cannot see it (pow(b,0)=1 for every b); freqs[1] can.
    (let f1ref (fpow 10000.0 (div -1.0 32.0)))
    (let f1got (fd-value (nth rung4 16) 8 23))
    (let f1ok (if (lt (div (abs (sub f1got f1ref)) f1ref) (dfb-tol)) 1 0))
    (let b524288 (if (eq b1 1)
        (if (eq (nth rung4 14) 78987094848)
            (if (eq (nth rung4 15) 1065353216) f1ok 0) 0) 0))
    (let b1048576 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (eq b524288 1)
        (if (eq (nth rung4 13) 896) (if (lt (nth rung4 11) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let b2097152 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (eq b524288 1)
        (if (lt (nth rung4 12) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    ; ── RUNG 6: inverse rope -> grouped output_a -> output_b (same chain, three more dispatches)
    ; facts 17.. : oaabs obabs oarows oacols obcols rank oaty obty nope6 relir relgrp relob
    (let b4194304 (if (eq b1 1)
        (if (eq (nth rung4 17) 78989329472)
            (if (eq (nth rung4 18) 79024981056)
                (if (eq (nth rung4 19) 8192)
